  "description": "with a 2000 Newest borrowed\nfrom Fuji. Please don't take this wrong, but a Newest costs about a third\nof what my own bikes do. It WORKS about 98% as well as my bikes do. The\ndifference is nearly imperceptible.\nHow can that be? I believe a medium-priced aluminum frame like the Newest's\ncustom butted 7005 alloy one is not very different from a much more expensive\naluminum one. I believe the construction methods and care are nearly the\nsame.\n\nI also believe that thanks to our friends at Shimano, parts groups like\nthe Newest's Tiagra are closer in action, weight and dependability to\nmore expensive groups than we ever dreamed possible. Brakes, shifting,\neverything.\n\nMy Newest had a Cro-moly steel fork, a 2002 will have an aluminum alloy\none, lighter and perhaps better-riding. A 2002 will have Vittoria tires\nand a CRP crankset with three aluminum rings. My Newest had one aluminum\nring, two steel ones.\n\nMost of the other parts remain the same as the ones on my bike, the three\nchainrings, the good wide-range (12-25) 9-speed gear cluster, the 32-spoke\nwheels, the clipless pedals.",
